  "learn": {
    "title": "Steady Threshold",
    "body": "Wire pot end1 to 5V, end2 to GND and wiper to A0. Wire D9 → 220 Ω → LED → GND. The knob runs from 0 to 1023 ADC counts.\n\nStart with the alarm off. Turn it on at a reading of 700 or above and off at 300 or below. Between those thresholds, keep the previous state. A single comparison with 500 cannot do this: the same midpoint must sometimes be on and sometimes off.\n\nRun and set the knob to 90%, then 50%, then 10%, then 50%. Pause at each setting for half a second. The LED must show on, on, off, off. Print ON or OFF only when the state changes. Keep reading A0 without a blocking delay.",
    "links": []
  },
